{
  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The best result so far (config_032, 0.6878 acc) uses scvi_n200 + ResNet50 in a multimodal setting, while the image-only ResNet50 baseline was very weak (0.2079 acc). This leaves a critical uncertainty: is the image modality contributing meaningfully, or is it limited by a weak encoder? Config_038 upgrades the image encoder to ViT-L (ImageNet-pretrained) while holding all other settings identical to config_032 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, concat), giving a clean single-variable comparison. If ViT-L substantially improves over ResNet50, it confirms the image modality has untapped potential and justifies further image-encoder exploration; if it does not, it tells us the image signal is inherently limited and we should focus remaining budget on RNA-side improvements or fusion. This is the highest-information experiment available because it resolves whether the second modality is a meaningful design axis at all, which governs the direction of all subsequent experiments."
}

